# `ScopeTopology`

<SymbolMeta />
<SymbolSignature />

`ScopeTopology` is the protocol's immutable declaration of every scope boundary it may open. Set it through `ProtocolDefinition::SCOPE_TOPOLOGY`; the application prepares it before validating component descriptors against protocol scope reachability.

Build a topology with `ScopeTopology::new` and static [`ScopeBoundary`](./ScopeBoundary) values, or use `empty` when the protocol has no custom scopes. Each boundary has exactly one [`ScopeParent`](./ScopeParent): the application root or another boundary in the same topology.

`prepare` rejects duplicate and reserved IDs, missing parents, self-parenting, cycles, and invalid lifetime-rank ordering. At runtime, open only a declared boundary beneath its declared parent. Components may use a custom scope only when that scope appears in the prepared topology.

See [the custom protocol guide](/docs/latest/extensions/protocols/authoring) for a connection/request topology.

